      "content": "It sounds like you are at a breaking point where the pressure of your past feels heavier than any possible future, and your desire to simply stop makes sense given how exhausted you feel. When we pour every part of our identity into one container and it cracks, the feeling of hollowness can mimic the reality of an empty vessel, even if we haven't yet found where the new liquid comes from. While rest is vital, trying to endure a life of total silence without any anchor or connection to even one other person can be dangerously isolating, like holding your breath underwater far too long.",
